{
  "manufacturer": "AAON",
  "manufacturer_slug": "aaon",
  "model": "VCM Controller (legacy, via PT-Link II BACnet gateway)",
  "model_slug": "vcm-pt-link-ii",
  "short_model": "VCM (PT-Link II)",
  "aliases": [
    "VCM",
    "AAON VCM",
    "PT-Link II",
    "PT-Link BACnet5",
    "G114680"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Rooftop unit / air handler controller (gateway)",
  "applies_to": "Older AAON units with the legacy VCM controller, reached through the AAON PT-Link II BACnet MS/TP gateway.",
  "summary": "AAON's PT-Link II BACnet5 gateway connects AAON controller loops to a BACnet MS/TP network. For the VCM controller it exposes 104 objects: setpoints, offsets and the schedule force as writable AVs, plus read-only temperatures, humidity, pressures, damper and VFD signals, unit mode, control status, enable flags and alarms.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": "50000 + MS/TP MAC address",
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Objects are served by the AAON PT-Link II gateway, which reads the controller over its RS-485 loop; object names are the PT-Link data names (SchdFrc, SpcTp and so on).",
    "Per the guide, AI and BI objects are read-only and AV objects are read/write; sensor inputs are read-only. No units column; AV limits are added to descriptions.",
    "Unit Mode and Control Status enumerations are listed in the guide's property identifier page; alarm group and relay objects are bit strings described there.",
    "The VCM is the legacy controller; its Control Status object is a bit string rather than an enumeration."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "PT-Link II BACnet5 Technical Guide - BACnet Properties and PT-Link Data Array Cross Reference for VCM",
    "doc_number": "G114680 Rev A",
    "revision_date": "2022-10-12",
    "url": "https://23126496.fs1.hubspotusercontent-na1.net/hubfs/23126496/G114680_PTLinkII_BACnet5_vA_221012.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Wire the PT-Link II to the AAON controller loop and to the BACnet MS/TP trunk, set its MAC address and baud rate, and check the device instance. The BAS schedules the unit with SchdFrc (AV 66) and adjusts the occupied and supply air setpoints; status, temperatures and alarms are read-only objects.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "AV 66",
        "name": "SchdFrc",
        "why": "Occupancy: 0 auto, 1 forced on, 2 forced off"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 42",
        "name": "OcpClSt",
        "why": "Occupied cooling mode enable setpoint"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 43",
        "name": "OcpHtSt",
        "why": "Occupied heating mode enable setpoint"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 77",
        "name": "SaClSt",
        "why": "Supply air cooling setpoint"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 78",
        "name": "SaHtSt",
        "why": "Supply air heating setpoint"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 123",
        "name": "UnitMode",
        "why": "Occupancy mode in effect"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 4",
        "name": "CtrlSts",
        "why": "Control status bits (demand, enables)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 72",
        "name": "SpcTp",
        "why": "Space temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 83",
        "name": "SaTp",
        "why": "Supply air temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 1",
        "name": "AlmSts",
        "why": "Summary of active alarm groups"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "SchdFrc (AV 66) sets occupancy: 0 = auto/unoccupied (the controller's own schedule and inputs decide), 1 = forced on, 2 = forced off.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "MS/TP MAC address must be 1-127; baud 9600, 19200, 38400 or 76800 is set on the PT-Link.",
      "Device instance = Device Instance ID (default 50,000) + MS/TP MAC address; change the ID on the PT-Link web Configuration page.",
      "The PT-Link web page defaults to 192.168.1.24 (user admin, password on the ProtoCessor label); AAON supports BACnet MS/TP only."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Alarm group and relay objects are bit-coded; decode them with the bit tables in the guide.",
      "Points for MODGAS, REHEAT, preheat and expansion boards report only when that hardware is connected."
    ]
  },
